WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.020
A newspaper column, in
a stern black headline:

2
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.360
our language is dying.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.670
Words fly off the page at you: lazy.

4
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.820
Crisis.

5
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.300
In my day.

6
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.940
Somewhere else, a linguist
opens a laptop to reply.

7
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.910
The page stays blank.

8
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.500
So what would a linguist actually say?

9
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.670
In this mission, you'll spot the
familiar ways people talk about language,

10
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.980
like decline, or a lost golden age.

11
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:33.920
You'll take a column apart word by word, to
see how it treats language, and teenagers.

12
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.230
And you'll plan the reply's
layout, part by part,

13
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.540
before a single word goes in.

14
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: work out
what a linguist would say.
